yeetNameCombos
// 💬 Yeet by username AND nickname — both regexes on the SAME line must match.
  // Format: /username regex/flags -- /nickname regex/flags
  // Identity order follows normal chat notation: [username](nickname)
  // Each line is one AND rule. Different lines are OR alternatives.
  // /^$/ means the field must be blank.
  //
  // Example combo (annotation only — not active):
  //   /jack/i -- /wolf/i
  //   [jack](wolf) -> match and yeet
  //   [jack](fox)  -> no match
  //   [bob](wolf)  -> no match
  //
  // Active special case below:
  //   [wolf](18+)  -> no match (username is not blank)
  //   [](wolf 18+) -> no match (nickname is not exactly 18+)
  //   [](18+)      -> match and yet

  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+$/i // Mr Dumb Question
  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+ ?straight$/i
  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+ ?\/he\/him$/i
  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+ ?He\/him$/i
  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+ ?\/straight\/he ?him$/i
  // /\^$/ -- /\^18\+ ?he\/straight$/i

